      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c828c7541558b0a3d0afeb2|full_name}: imagine being able to color code them, it could significantly add new versatility or challenges to world creation \nFor example you a have a room with a bat and a button, you try to use the bat but the bat gives a red flare around it, you can't grab it but you could if yoh can activate it, and pressing the button would allow you pick it up and now it is a blue flare\n\n\nIts not like the presented idea but it adds a layer of sophistication to it\nAnother example could be that you have 100 buttons and the bat, looking at the bat will give a red flare but one of the buttons will have a white flare when the bat is highlighted, adding a new gameplay method",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
